      "prompt": "Use case: original first-grade Chinese reading storybook illustrations, no text. Create one full-bleed atlas, EXACTLY three columns by two rows of equal square panels. Each panel fully independent with no object crossing a boundary, critical subjects near center and away from outer 6 percent. Fine paper grain, matte gouache, clean cut-paper contours, deep pine greens and warm cream, muted pond turquoise and apricot/persimmon accents. Calm atmosphere, instantly readable thumbnail focal shapes. NO words, letters, numbers, diagrams, musical notation, drawn arrows or watermark. Original character and layout design, do not mimic any textbook page. \nTOP LEFT: a child with a short warm orange scarf and pine-green vest looks curiously from a quiet wooden boardwalk at a very large round green lotus LEAF in a small pond. Show a nearly continuous circular outline, gentle radiating leaf veins and a slender upright stem from below, no wedge notch and no large flowers obscuring it. One pink bud far in the background is optional. \nTOP CENTER: an entirely different scene close-up; one glossy round blue-turquoise anthropomorphic water droplet reclines comfortably near the center of a gently cupped round green lotus leaf above the pond. The character has two tiny dark eyes, simple warm face and one pronounced small white shine highlight. A relaxed tilt suggests lying down. Show the green leaf as a gently curved cradle-like surface, no wooden cradle in this panel.\nTOP RIGHT: an original coral orange-bodied dragonfly with one slender segmented tail, standing ON a round green lotus leaf, feet visibly contacting it. It has four partly transparent pale blue wings clearly extended outward in two pairs, with visible subtle vein lines. Camera at three-quarter angle shows the spread wings and body large, nothing else.\nBOTTOM LEFT: one sage green frog squatting on a round lotus leaf above calm water, two bent hind legs visibly folded and open mouth as it sings. Front perspective, single large friendly frog, no other characters, no text or music glyphs.\nBOTTOM CENTER: a clear side-on storybook scene shows an orange small fish swimming UNDER a raised round green lotus leaf, the leaf on its curved tall stem in the upper portion, broad green circular canopy above the fish. Fish fully visible in the turquoise water below, facing right, with a few little light splashes. One fish only. The separation of ABOVE leaf and BELOW water is unmistakable. \nBOTTOM RIGHT: neutral wooden tabletop in a cozy home, one simple long flat deep blue ribbon laid horizontally and one clearly round yellow wool ball placed well apart next to it. Make their shape and color easy to recognize as two different objects. No written labels, no hands, uncluttered and spacious."
    },
