      "prompt": "Use case: separate transparent sprite illustrations for an original first-grade Chinese reading game. Make exactly 3 columns x 3 rows of independent equal square cells, each object centered and at most 65 percent of its cell, transparent margin separating every asset. True alpha transparency, no shadows or glowing backdrop. Fine paper grain, matte gouache, clean cut-paper shapes, deep pine green, warm cream, soft pond turquoise, orange and persimmon accents. Strong silhouette recognizable when tiny. No words, letters, arrows, numeric marks, musical notes or watermark.\nTOP LEFT: one round turquoise water droplet with two tiny dark eyes, one tiny smile and clear white gleam at upper left. One cohesive almost circular shape, no leaf or other prop. TOP CENTER: one orange coral dragonfly in wide top three-quarter view, four pale blue partly transparent wings visibly spread out and one slender body, no leaf or prop. TOP RIGHT: one cheerful crouching sage-green frog with folded legs and two big round eyes, simple silhouette.\nMIDDLE LEFT: one small orange fish in profile facing right, clear tail and fins, no water or prop. MIDDLE CENTER: one tiny warm apricot wooden rocking cradle, curved rocker bottom, simple railing and cream blanket, empty and with no baby. MIDDLE RIGHT: one circular flat concrete landing pad with simple cream outer perimeter stripe and one tiny green toy helicopter visibly settled on it; has slender rotors and landing skids, no H, letters or numbers.\nBOTTOM LEFT: one original little teal singing stage with shallow circular raised base and single amber microphone on a dark-green stand, no performer. BOTTOM CENTER: one open green sun umbrella angled slightly from the side with simple handle, unmistakable shade canopy, no person. BOTTOM RIGHT: one warm cream completion sticker with a round green lotus leaf silhouette and one persimmon dot, simple paper badge without words. Separate original art on genuine transparency."
