      "prompt": "Use case: six original separate alpha PNG sprites for a first-grade lotus-pond Chinese classroom. One atlas of exactly 3 columns and 2 rows. Equal well-separated cells, objects occupy only 62 percent of their own cell, transparent margins, no overlaps or cast shadows or particles. Pine green, cream, muted pond teal, apricot and persimmon orange. Fine paper grain, matte gouache, crisp paper-cut silhouettes readable when tiny. No words, text, numbers, arrows or watermarks.\nTOP LEFT: side view of a little pond push vehicle, a compact warm cream boat-shaped cart with TWO visible round deep-green wheels and a persimmon-orange short prow pointing RIGHT. Low stable cargo bay and no passengers. \nTOP MIDDLE: the exact same tiny boat-shaped push cart, same two wheels and dimensions, second motion frame with a small green pennant visibly tilted to the left above rear cargo bay. No glowing trail or dust. \nTOP RIGHT: one large round softly glossy turquoise-blue glass marble with a single cream gleam at top left, simple circle ball shape, no face or shadow.\nBOTTOM LEFT: exactly one round warm orange ball, an almost perfect sphere with tiny muted grain, no highlight that changes apparent orange color, no features. \nBOTTOM MIDDLE: exactly one round muted violet-purple ball, same silhouette and size as orange ball, no other objects.\nBOTTOM RIGHT: exactly one long thin orange ribbon lying flat, stretched horizontally, obvious rectangular length at least 4 times its width, no curled ends or marks.\nKeep original art simple with transparent backgrounds, no fake gray checkerboard, no scene framing."
