      "prompt": "Use case: four independently cropped alpha PNG sprites for an original Chinese first-grade story quiz. One strictly equal 2-column x 2-row sheet, with genuine transparent empty margins surrounding every object. No background colors, text, words, numbers, musical signs, border or drawn arrows. Fine paper grain, matte gouache and clean cut-paper contours. Warm sage, pine green, pond blue and cream, subtle apricot touches, one original simple paper puppet character. Do not reference any textbook.\nTOP LEFT: a sage-green small frog puppet with two large eyes, seen front-left three-quarter, both back legs clearly folded tight under body in a crouch, forefeet touching ground, face looking slightly upward with CLOSED mouth rendered as one thin smile line and no visible interior. No external leaf or water.\nTOP RIGHT: exactly the same frog puppet in the same crouching pose but its mouth is clearly WIDE OPEN in a happy singing expression with visibly dark mouth interior and tiny pink tongue. Add two very short curved cream-orange sound marks near mouth, no musical notes or text.\nBOTTOM LEFT: the same frog puppet leaping upward, both long back legs fully extended below and apart, forefeet lifted and eyes looking upward. Distinct visibly AIRBORNE pose. No motion lines necessary.\nBOTTOM RIGHT: a single nearly circular broad flat green lotus leaf viewed obliquely, as a horizontal canopy with a small gentle curl along its rim and thin radial veins; one slender curved upright stem connects at center and extends downward. No notch, no water, no flower or extra object. \nAll four objects keep transparent gaps around them, smaller than 70 percent of their own cell."
